      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Program & Student Support (CIPGS)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The College of Innovative Professional and Graduate Studies (CIPGS) is seeking a dependable, professional, and student-focused graduate student to serve as a Graduate Student Assistant supporting the college's front office, student services, residency activities, and special projects. This person will serve as one of the first points of contact for students, prospective students, faculty, staff, and visitors who come to the CIPGS office. The position requires someone who is welcoming and approachable while also able to work independently, exercise good judgment, and recognize when a question or concern should be directed to a member of the CIPGS staff. In addition to front-office responsibilities, the graduate assistant will support activities associated with CIPGS's high- and low-residency programs. Responsibilities may include assisting with student arrival and check-in, intake activities, preparing materials and packets, setting up meeting spaces, greeting students and faculty, and providing logistical support during residency activities. The position will also provide opportunities to assist with college and program projects based on the student's skills, knowledge, and interests and the needs of the college. These projects may include administrative support, event preparation, communications, data organization, research, or other activities that contribute to the work of CIPGS. The ideal candidate is friendly without needing to be constantly supervised, confident enough to help people find answers, and thoughtful enough to know when to ask for help. The student should enjoy interacting with people, pay attention to details, and be willing to step away from routine front-office responsibilities to contribute to projects and activities that support CIPGS.   Responsibilities: Serve as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for current and prospective graduate students, faculty, staff, and visitors to the CIPGS office. Provide basic information and directions and help students and visitors connect with the appropriate CIPGS staff member or university office. Assist students with navigating university resources and systems. Help students understand where to go or whom to contact when questions fall outside the scope of the graduate assistant's responsibilities. Maintain an organized, welcoming, and professional front-office environment. Assist with routine administrative and office tasks as needed. Assist with preparation for high- and low-residency activities. Help prepare student packets, materials, meeting spaces, and other resources. Assist with student arrival, check-in, and intake activities. Greet and assist students participating in residency activities. Provide logistical support to faculty and staff during residency events and meetings. Assist with other activities designed to create a welcoming and well-organized experience for residency students. Assist CIPGS faculty and staff with special projects and initiatives. Contribute to programmatic or college-level projects based on the student's skills, knowledge, and interests. Assist with event preparation, communications, data organization, research, or other projects as assigned. Handle student, faculty, program, and institutional information in accordance with university confidentiality, FERPA, and data privacy expectations. Identify appropriate tasks and take initiative during periods when front-office activity is limited. Performs additional job-related duties and responsibilities as requested.   Qualifications: Admitted to and enrolled in an Avila University graduate program.  Current Avila University student in good academic and conduct standing. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Professional, welcoming, and comfortable interacting with a diverse population of students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Strong attention to detail. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise appropriate judgment. Ability to work independently and take initiative. Reliable and able to manage responsibilities with minimal supervision. Comfortable learning and using university technology and systems. Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities.  Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law.   You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)” and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.cloud.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f2ab6114-2e48-45a8-8ffc-c90819d5d7ff&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=145458603_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Student Success Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\n\nLocation: Kansas City\n\nPosition Summary The Student Success Coach Graduate Assistant works one-on-one with students who need additional academic support. The GA will help students identify challenges, develop strategies for improvement, and connect with appropriate university resources. Tuition remission for 12 graduate credit hours per academic year (6 fall, 6 spring).  This is an in-person position requiring 220 working hours during the academic year. The weekly schedule is flexible and will be determined with the supervisor based on the GA’s class schedule and departmental needs. Once established, the schedule should remain consistent throughout the semester. Responsibilities: Meet individually with students to provide academic success coaching. Help students develop skills related to: Time management and prioritization Study skills Goal setting Communicating with professors Balancing academic and personal commitments Creating plans to catch up when falling behind Building academic confidence Connect students with appropriate campus resources and support services. Provide outreach to students identified through Navigate alerts, progress reports, midterm grades, and other Student Success initiatives. Record student meeting notes and outreach in Navigate. Participate in training and meetings with the Student Success team as needed. Perform other job-related duties as assigned by supervisor.    Qualifications: Must be admitted and enrolled in a graduate program at Avila University. International students are not eligible for graduate assistantships. The successful candidate for this position will possess a bachelor's degree and must maintain a minimum 3.0 GPA, a commitment to student development, higher education, creativity, vision, passion, and compassion are imperative. Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to work effectively one-on-one with students Strong organization and time-management skills Ability to maintain confidentiality and professional boundaries Experience working with college students is preferred but not required The Office of Student Success Graduate Assistant position involves substantial direct involvement with students and staff in various capacities, as such it is expected that the GA must conduct themselves as a professional staff member while in the office which includes dress, behavior, and attitude.  Project assignment will be consistent with needs, interests and expertise. The GA is expected to work the appropriate number of hours based on the allotted hours stated in the Graduate Assistant policy. The term of this position is based on the availability of the successful candidate but shall not exceed two full academic years.  Successful candidates should showcase their work and experience in contributing to a climate that supports a diverse student body, serves first-generation college students, multilingual learners, and contributions to equity and social justice through their work. The Community: Kansas City, a two-state metropolitan area with a population of nearly two million, offers a wide variety of cultural, educational and social life opportunities.  Avila University, a Catholic university founded and inspired by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet, provides undergraduate and graduate education in the liberal arts and professional studies, preparing lifelong learners who make meaningful contributions to the global community. Additional Employment Information: Avila University is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate on the basis of, sex, race, religion, age, color, sexual orientation, disability, national or ethnic origin, marital status, veteran's status, genetic information or any other characteristic protected by law.   You must be at least 18 years of age to be employed by Avila University. All new employees will be required to complete an \"Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9)” and produce requested documentation after employment. In compliance with the Higher Education Amendments of 1998, the university's annual security and crime statistics report is available at https://www.avila.edu/campus-resources/campus-safety.&nbsp ; A copy of this report is available upon request from the Campus Safety Office in the Whitfield building any weekday between 8am and 5pm. Avila University requires the successful completion of a background check as a condition of employment.",
